# Build context for ./Dockerfile (the repository root).
# Above all never in an image: a developer's .env files (real keys) and
# services/api/var/ (uploaded resumes, generated documents, evaluation captures).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
services/api/var/
*.dump

# Rebuilt inside the image, or not needed there.
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.next-e2e/
**/.next-ext-e2e/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.artifacts/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# Tests, evaluation, docs and the extension: the image serves the web app and
# the API only. (apps/web/e2e stays: the web build type-checks
# playwright.config.ts, which imports from it.) The extension's package.json stays, because the lockfile names
# it as a workspace and `npm ci` checks the two agree.
services/api/tests/
services/api/evaluation/
apps/extension/*
!apps/extension/package.json
docs/
PROJECT.md
infrastructure/
tests/
